I added `WithTax` to `pricing/tax.go` and a `TestWithTax` test in `pricing/tax_test.go`. The full suite passes (`go test ./...`), and `gofmt` and `go vet` are clean.

```go
// WithTax returns amount with the sales tax of region r added. A tax-exempt
// customer pays no tax, so amount comes back unchanged.
func WithTax(amount Money, r Region, exempt bool) Money {
	return amount + Tax(amount, r, exempt)
}
```

The signature mirrors `Tax`, so the rounding and exemption rules come from `Tax` and are not duplicated. The test covers a Quebec amount (10,000 becomes 11,498), a small amount, zero, a negative amount (unchanged), and the tax-free path is covered by the exempt case in `TestTaxExempt`.

I did not add `WithTax` to `REQUIREMENTS.md`. R-TAX-RATE and R-TAX-EXEMPT already name `Tax` as their code, so if you want `WithTax` traced to a requirement, that entry needs updating.
